  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Reported by Ross against 3.0b1 Apr 2, 2008.  The problem also exists in maintenance-2.2.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Our library is overhauling our web site and web site tools and one of the new web page editor tools is called Contribute from Adobe. We ran into a problem where people were using Contribute to cut/paste citation URLs that were referencing Fedora dissemination requests. Contribute takes URLs that look like:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://repo.lib.virginia.edu:18080/fedora/get/uva-lib:32653/uva-lib-bdef:100/getFullView"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://repo.lib.virginia.edu:18080/fedora/get/uva-lib:32653/uva-lib-bdef:100/getFullView",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "and properly escapes special characters like the colon so the URL is rewritten as:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://repo.lib.virginia.edu:18080/fedora/get/uva-lib%3A32653/uva-lib-bdef%3A100/getFullView"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://repo.lib.virginia.edu:18080/fedora/get/uva-lib%3A32653/uva-lib-bdef%3A100/getFullView",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Problem is, Fedora cannot handle the rewritten URL. The bug is in the request URL parsing section of FedoraAccessServlet where it is looking for a colon(",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "id": "1f642",
        "shortName": ":slight_smile:",
        "text": "🙂"
       },
       "type": "emoji"
      },
      {
       "text": " character but fails to URLDecode the string before it does the lookup. The result is that %3A does not match colon(",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "id": "1f642",
        "shortName": ":slight_smile:",
        "text": "🙂"
       },
       "type": "emoji"
      },
      {
       "text": " when parsing the bdef pid section of the URL so the conditional incorrectly fails.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "There are two places in code where:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "if (URIArray[6].indexOf(\":\") == -1) {",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "should instead be",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "if (URLDecoder.decode(URIArray[6], \"UTF-8\").indexOf(\":\") == -1) {",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
