      "displayName": "Stephen Bayliss",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>No longer covered by the implementation of \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-627\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-627\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Fedora REST-style object viewer does not properly handle encoded slashes in the pid value.\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10303?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-627\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n - this is now a separate issue.</p>\n\n<p>The API-A LITE does not accept URL-encoded PIDs, however the new REST API does (and requires them to be encoded).  One solution could be to point people at the new REST API and let them use that instead.  Alternatively we could consider some limited handling of URL-encoding in API-A LITE (but being careful not to break any existing behaviour).</p>",
